  "hypotheses": [
    "A factory-only request verifier can close the canonical request envelope and detached payload, deployment binding, controller generation, operation identity, correlation, authority-vector shape, request window, payload hash, and null-projection request hash before mutation verification consumes the exact retained request.",
    "A factory-only mutation verifier can bind that request to the retained publication read set and durable commit context, reconstruct COMMITTED N+6 mutations or exact NO_CHANGE zero writes, and retain the operation-result schema/envelope blocker until a final result context is verified.",
    "A factory-only repository receipt verifier can replay the exact mutation and nonce query, bind exact canonical transaction and row-artifact hashes, seven write-count categories, four-authority CAS, branch-specific commit clocks and current CONTROL_REPOSITORY_EVIDENCE Ed25519 authority while keeping every unresolved target blocker explicit and forbidding post-commit digest back-references.",
    "A factory-only successful-result verifier can replay the mutation closure and exact-project the detached result payload, post-state authority, committed version set, closed pre-existing receipt set, policy hash, correlation, completion window, payload hash, and null-projection result hash without feeding result bytes back into the commit DAG.",
    "Consistent fixtures, locally generated role signatures, and deterministic replay prove component algorithms only. They cannot prove target transport acceptance, endpoint/session identity, durable nonce ownership, idempotency ownership, a real SERIALIZABLE repository implementation or clocks, atomic visibility, post-anchor outbox delivery, authentic result exchange, target mapping/build/runner execution, or product authorization."
